                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Wow - I cannot believe this game has overwhelmingly positive reviews.  Here's the biggest con - it ends with major plot points being unresolved.  Given that this game was made over a decade ago and the developer himself said he didn't know how to resolve it via a sequel, it is extremely unsatisfying.  Imagine something akin to the Game of Thrones series or the Kingkiller Chronicles with unfinished endings.\n\nThe game takes a lot from Ace Attorney - specifically the courtroom scenes.  You ask people questions and when they say two statements that contradict each other - you point that out.  You get clarifications and new clues and you move forward with trying to resolve the mystery.\n\nThe beginning and up the the middle is very good.  Great video direction and the performances are solid.  Some actors are more theatrical than others, and while I liked the more realistic acting, I didn't mind this.\n\nHowever, somewhere during the middle I got a sense of unease.  I was stuck and checked out the tips which asked me to follow up with a character because I didn't ask him about several pieces of evidence.  But in the game you seem him being preoccupied and basically he says he'll be busy for the hour.  I later found out that I was supposed to be finding a contradiction with a different person.  I started losing trust in the direction of the game.\n\nAnd sure enough as the game went on, it got increasingly more outrageous and there was less time left till the game was going to finish.  The contradictions started being less clever and more asinine, and I sighed as the credits rolled as true to my concerns, it ended extremely unsatisfactorily.  There's this method that Agatha Christie and JJ Abrahams (Lost) uses in storytelling where they create increasingly intriguing situations without knowing the true culprit and by the time they reach the ending they put in the most surprising person as the suspect.  However, this style of storytelling only works if they land the ending, which this game did not.\n\nPlease don't waste your time with this game.  It has good ideas, but ultimately doesn't live up to its potential.",
